seg-a0011b278269 = The <c1/> kind answers: for a spacecraft above, around or far past the GNSS orbits, how many GNSS signals can it use, how strong are they, how good is the geometry, and what can an onboard filter do with them? It has three modes, chosen by which table the scenario has: <c2/>, <c3/> or <c4/> (with an optional <c5/>).

# text
seg-2e4ac6b7a883 = Status: <b>MODELLED</b>. The availability sweeps are compared with the ICG Space Service Volume booklet under a pre-registration; see <a1>what the comparison shows</a1> before relying on any number.

