seg-a0ff58bccaa8 = Public sources

# text
# c1: xval/gnss-ssv/fetch.sh
seg-4658268e82e1 = <em>The Interoperable Global Navigation Satellite Systems Space Service Volume</em>, United Nations Office for Outer Space Affairs, ST/SPACE/75 ({ "1" } November { "2018" }), prepared by the International Committee on GNSS (ICG), Working Group B: the method (annex B), the orbital elements of every constellation (annex C), the transmit beamwidths and powers (tables B2, B6, B8, { "4.2" }), the user antennas (table B10), and the published availability tables. It is itself a simulation. Fetched by <c1/> (pinned SHA-256), never vendored.

# text
seg-e46d9353e6f3 = U.S. Coast Guard Navigation Center, GPS Block IIR and IIR-M antenna panel patterns (Marquis, { "2014" }): the measured L1 panel patterns used only to judge the parametric stand-in (bar S7). Fetched, never vendored, no pattern data committed.

# text
# c1: src/ssv/limb.rs
seg-0a002dc0df64 = The constants of the model (gravity, Earth rotation, free-space loss, noise density) are standard; the Gallagher plasmasphere density law, the Chapman layer and the radio refractivity profile are published forms, used with stated simple parameters (see <c1/>).

# text
seg-c3c3f63df966 = Shell mode: the booklet's global metric

# text
# c1: [shell]
seg-f1e153c95b13 = <c1/> places a user on a sphere (default { "36,000" } km altitude with a nadir-pointing hemispherical antenna, the upper SSV; or { "8,000" } km with an omnidirectional antenna, the lower SSV) on a 2,562-point icosphere grid and counts, over { "14" } days at 1-minute steps, the share of (user, epoch) pairs with at least one and at least four signals, per constellation and combined, and the longest outage at the worst user. The sweep uses the closed-form visibility interval in central angle (a beam cone, Earth blockage by the { "6378" } km sphere plus { "50" } km, the user hemisphere and the RF range limit) and runs in seconds in a release build; a property test checks it against the general geometric predicate.

# attr:alt
seg-1f79a5aae6c5 = Signal availability for a user on a sphere at { "36000" } km altitude with a hemisphere antenna, from a real run of engine v{ $version } on scenarios/gnss-ssv-shell.toml (a reduced run: { "162" } users, { "3" } days, { "10" } min steps), at a { "20" } dB-Hz threshold. For each constellation and band, two bars: the share of (user, epoch) pairs with at least one signal and with at least four. Combined, L1: { "99.4" } % at least one, { "73.2" } % at least four, longest outage below four signals { "160" } min. Combined, L5: { "100.0" } % at least one, { "99.9" } % at least four, longest outage below four signals { "20" } min. MODELLED: a modelled study from stated inputs, not a measurement and not a service-volume claim for any system. The reduced size is not the booklet comparison. Advisory: analysis output from a research and engineering tool, not type-approved navigation equipment and not a safety-of-life service.

