seg-3fb4c06c8b3f = Trajectory mode: along an orbit

# text
# c1: [trajectory]
# c2: leo
# c3: meo
# c4: geo
# c5: heo
# c6: lunar-transfer
seg-632fedc95af5 = <c1/> flies the user on a Keplerian orbit (a preset: <c2/>, <c3/>, <c4/>, <c5/> (the booklet's table { "5.10" }) or <c6/>, or elements) and reports, per band and constellation, availability of one and four signals, outage durations, signals in view, best C/N0, dilution of precision (median, 95th percentile, worst), links received through the main lobe and through sidelobes, and an optional time series and CSV.

# text
# c1: [transmit] pattern
# c2: booklet
# c3: parametric
# c4: table
# c5: pattern_csv
# c6: pattern_text
# c7: xval/gnss-ssv/extract_patterns.py
seg-7bfd301cd789 = <b>Transmit pattern</b> (<c1/>): <c2/> (constant power inside the reference off-boresight angle), <c3/> (a labelled stand-in: { "3" } dB per degree beyond the reference angle to a floor { "25" } dB below the main lobe; <b>not</b> any system's measured pattern) or <c4/> (a measured pattern you supply: <c5/> or inline <c6/>; the Block IIR/IIR-M panel patterns can be extracted with <c7/>).

# text
seg-c1390929d9f2 = <b>Receive antennas</b>: omni, hemisphere, or the booklet's table-B10 high-gain and patch antennas, nadir or zenith; each link uses the antenna with the higher gain.

# text
# c1: [atmosphere]
seg-fe56ab7a2cac = <b>Limb-ray medium</b> (<c1/>): a Chapman ionosphere, a plasmasphere (Gallagher { "1988" } form, plasmapause at L = { "4.5" }, tapered below { "1,500" } km) and a neutral atmosphere (bending about { "1.33" } degrees at the surface, oxygen absorption, defocusing) integrated along the straight ray. Reports slant TEC, the plasmaspheric part, excess delay, tangent altitude and the links lost to grazing. Straight-ray integration: bending is reported, not iterated.

# text
# c1: [receiver] weak_signal
seg-1bad91204f6a = <b>Weak-signal receiver</b> (<c1/>): coherent and non-coherent integration, data-bit limit, aiding and pilot channels, Doppler search; the acquisition threshold at the stated detection and false-alarm probabilities and the carrier and code tracking thresholds replace the fixed C/N0 threshold ({ "10" } to { "25" } dB-Hz range). Reuses the engine's acquisition and tracking-loop models.

# attr:alt
seg-92ef8e0b78de = Signals along one high Earth orbit (perigee { "497" } km, apogee { "58622" } km, period { "18.8" } h), from a real run of engine v{ $version } on scenarios/gnss-ssv-heo.toml, band L1. Top: the best carrier-to-noise density among the signals in view, against the { "20" } dB-Hz threshold. Middle: the number of signals in view from all constellations, from { "4" } to { "55" } along the sampled points. Of the links received, { "2252" } came through a main lobe and { "696" } through sidelobes, using a labelled parametric stand-in pattern, not any system's measured pattern. Median PDOP { "67" }, 95th percentile { "358" }. MODELLED: a modelled study from stated inputs, not a measurement and not a service-volume claim for any system. Advisory: analysis output from a research and engineering tool, not type-approved navigation equipment and not a safety-of-life service.

